WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.120
- He's an American entrepreneur,

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:03.770
author and speaker.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.100
He's widely respected as one

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.600
of the world's most well known

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.880
and respected internet marketers.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.260
He teaches through a
mix of video training,

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.760
webinars written, guides,
one-on-one training

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:14.990
and seminars.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:15.990
He's Eben Pagan

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.157
and here his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:21.745 --> 00:00:24.460
- He says rich is a state of mind.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:27.340
And that if you're rich on the inside

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.340
you can then go create money

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.460
but if you're not rich on the inside,

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.440
if you don't have a rich state of mind

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.280
not only will you not be able to attract

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.280
and create money

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.030
but if you do get some

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.620
you'll find a way to get rid of it.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.050
Right a way that I have of seeing it

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.890
is that there's a big difference

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:48.510
between money and wealth.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.250
And wealth comes

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.080
from having knowledge,

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.780
systems, assets, understanding

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:00.929
of how to create value for others

00:01:00.929 --> 00:01:01.920
and having systems

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.300
and assets that create value

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.920
whereas money is just these

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.250
you know imaginary numbers

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.740
and these worthless pieces of paper

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.970
that we you know try to pretend

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.010
to have value.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:16.510
So success is about fulfillment.

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.630
And I think fulfillment

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:20.170
is about creating success for yourself

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:22.280
but then creating success for others

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:23.550
in helping them succeed.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.760
Have you ever seen Stephen Covey

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:26.760
talking about how

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:29.280
you have to put the big rocks in your day

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.490
or else they they won't go in.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.820
And so what he'll do is

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:33.900
he takes a big fish tank

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.280
and on the table he has some big rocks

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.120
and then he has some smaller rocks

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:39.700
and then he has some pebbles

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:40.740
and then he has some sand.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.030
Okay and so what he does

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.480
is first he starts by putting

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.710
all the sand into the tank

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.300
and then he puts in the little pebbles

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.570
and then he puts in the bigger rocks

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:51.700
and by the time he's done

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:53.160
the tank is almost full

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:56.040
and he can't fit in the
big rocks that he has.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.050
They just kind of sit on top

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.240
and there's nowhere to put most of them.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.240
But then what he does

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.240
is he takes the big rocks

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.450
and he puts them into the tank first

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.430
and then he takes the smaller rocks

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:05.430
and he he puts them in

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:06.710
and he fits them around the bigger rocks.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:08.150
Then he takes the little pebbles

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:09.150
and he puts them in

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.780
and they fit in around
the the smaller rocks

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:11.780
and the bigger ones.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:14.150
And then he pours a ton of sand in there

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:16.340
which fills all the cracks up.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.510
And the lesson is

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:20.700
that you have to put
in the big rocks first

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.230
or else they'll never go in.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:26.430
Okay and the interesting
thing about the big rocks

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:29.620
is that they have to be chosen in advance.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.950
In other words you must identify

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:34.280
what your most valuable activities are

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:37.590
and then install them in
your day ahead of time

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.450
because if you don't, okay,

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:42.090
other people will have
things for you to do.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.180
Other people will take your attention.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.990
And I can almost guarantee you

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:47.010
that these other things

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:49.950
that other people have
for you are less important

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:50.950
but in the moment

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:52.680
they seem a lot more urgent.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.870
Okay so you got to put
the big rocks in first

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:56.960
and very importantly

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.740
you have to know what they are.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.750
Don't keep your best ideas secret.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:03.180
Most of the business owners that I know

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.840
whenever they figure out something

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:05.840
that's really fantastic,

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:08.430
a thing that would
really help prospects out

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:09.680
they start scheming

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:11.990
about how to sell it for a lot of money

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:13.090
and about how to get people

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:14.260
to give them money

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.320
before they reveal this secret to them

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:17.540
or this product or this service

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.590
or this this information.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:21.700
Well guess what?

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.290
If you don't show people what you've got

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:25.490
and you don't prove to them

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.710
that you have a lot of value

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:28.760
they're not going to
pay any attention to you

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:29.960
at all.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.450
A different mindset that I've developed

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.950
and learned over the last several years

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.450
is that if you will take your best ideas,

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.330
the ones that are the most valuable,

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:40.400
the ones that you might consider

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.770
to be the silver bullets,

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:44.090
the magic bullets,

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.710
the ones that work every time,

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:47.310
that give instant results,

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:48.320
that eliminate hassle

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:51.100
and friction from a person's life,

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.840
and you give those away,

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.460
the prospect will say to themselves

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.960
oh geez if this is what they're giving way

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.280
how much better must be the product

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.340
that they're selling?

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.430
So the advice that I have for you is

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:05.510
ask yourself right now

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:08.650
what is the one thing
that you've figured out

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:09.700
over your lifetime

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:11.010
and over your career

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:13.960
that can help your prospects out the most?

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:16.510
The thing that can give
them the most value,

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:17.600
eliminate the most friction

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.010
and hassle from their life,

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:20.790
alright the thing that works,

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:22.000
every single time.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.000
What's the magic bullet

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.000
that you figured out?

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.500
The one that before you heard this

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.380
you would never share with anyone.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:29.380
Okay good.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:30.470
What I'd like you to do now

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:33.520
is make a commitment to
yourself to give it away

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.370
and give it away to as many people

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.210
as you possibly can.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.210
By the way this is the kind of thing

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.580
that will create viral marketing for you.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:41.870
This is the kind of thing that

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:42.870
you give it away

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:44.580
people will start talking about it.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:45.660
They'll start coming to you

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.410
and saying wow that's an incredible idea,

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:48.830
do you have any more?

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:50.870
And I advise you to give away even more

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:52.360
of your good ideas.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:54.280
Now language is part of communication

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:55.520
but there's a much bigger piece

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:58.080
of communication than language

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:01.020
which is the nonverbal communication

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:02.960
that happens between people.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:05.260
Most persuasion, most bonding,

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:07.470
most connection happens on channels

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.220
other than the words.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.210
Right so you've heard
the the old estimates

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.550
that you know over 90%

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:13.680
of your communication

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.000
is your voice tone and your body language.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.280
Communication is so important.

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:20.770
And what's amazing is most people

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:21.770
are just unconscious.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:23.160
They're not paying any attention to it.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:24.720
They're not learning how to communicate

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.250
with and connect with other people better.

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:28.150
So learn about body language.

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:30.210
Learn about nonverbal communication.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:31.580
Learn about how to connect with people

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.270
and build rapport.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.340
So I think of entrepreneurship

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:37.840
as being like an ultimate training ground,

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:40.250
an ultimate practice place

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.840
to learn the basic skills
that we need to learn

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:45.530
in order to then come back

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:47.830
and be great at contribution.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:49.660
Steven Covey has the model

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:52.780
of first we start out dependent

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:54.910
and then we become independent

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:58.120
and then we become interdependent.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.720
And in developmental models

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.630
if you study developmental psychology

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:04.220
which I recommend you do

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:06.190
in any of the developmental models

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:09.380
each level acts as a foundation

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:12.080
for the next level.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:14.720
So if we don't become
powerfully independent

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:18.370
we can't become powerfully interdependent.

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:19.500
And I think of entrepreneurship

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.580
as being the best school now

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:26.090
for becoming powerfully independent.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:28.710
Robert Kiyosaki who
wrote Rich Dad Poor Dad

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:29.830
and Cash Flow Quadrant

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:30.830
and some other books

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:33.720
that are excellent initial training,

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:35.710
he's got this model where he says

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:38.000
we start out as employee

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.860
and then we go to self-employed

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:41.370
and then we become business owners

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:43.380
and then we become investors

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.380
and then I would add

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.130
then we become philanthropists ideally,

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:47.130
we'd become people

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.720
to come back and contribute.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.220
And these build upon each other.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:53.590
Okay so when you're an employee

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:56.110
you learn some tasks some skills.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:57.110
You do them.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:58.110
You get a paycheck.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:06:59.270
When you become self-employed

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:00.270
now you're responsible.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:02.180
You have to go get the business as well.

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:04.370
Then when you're a business owner

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:07.050
you create that organism or that entity

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:09.690
that then runs and throws off the profit.

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:11.280
And then when you become an investor

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:13.860
you invest in those types of entities.

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:15.050
And then ideally

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:16.080
when you become a philanthropist

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.440
or someone that's contributing

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.960
you start investing in the most important

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:23.979
you know biggest widest
scale kind of projects.

00:07:23.979 --> 00:07:26.010
And I say that model, those five steps,

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:27.470
because entrepreneur, business owner

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:29.300
is in the middle.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:30.650
And what I want to emphasize

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:32.810
is that entrepreneurship

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:34.540
and owning and building a business,

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:37.910
it's one step in a much bigger puzzle.

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:39.870
It's not the end.

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:40.870
And unfortunately

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:42.840
I see a lot of entrepreneurs get stuck

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:44.280
at that step.

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:45.280
They get to that level

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:47.180
and they start becoming very successful

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:48.680
and then they just want more

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:49.680
and bigger

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:50.680
and you know more money

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:52.030
and more power

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:53.520
rather than realizing

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:54.720
oh that's just one step

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:56.740
that I need to become competent in

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:58.330
so that I can go on to the next level

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.790
and go on to the next level.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:00.790
So what's the difference

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:01.790
between these levels?

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:05.160
Well essentially the difference is

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:08.150
each one becomes more complex

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:09.990
and more multi-dimensional

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:11.830
and has a longer time horizon.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:13.650
Alright so when you're an employee

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:14.650
you're just doing your work

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:15.960
to get your paycheck in two weeks.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:17.840
When you're self-employed

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:19.500
all of a sudden the time horizon moves out

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:21.520
and you learn about invoicing

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:24.370
and you learn that
companies don't pay invoices

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:26.680
as fast as you used to get your paycheck.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.270
And then when you become a business owner,

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:31.960
an entrepreneur you know kind of proper,

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:33.050
you start thinking in timeframes

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:35.960
of months and in years in terms of return.

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:36.960
You become an investor.

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:38.710
You start thinking in
terms of multiple years

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:40.060
or even decades.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:41.570
And then philanthropist,

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:44.740
you know you look way
out onto the horizon.

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:46.760
And I say this because

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:48.540
because each level builds

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.610
on the previous levels

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:51.740
this entrepreneur level

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:54.830
where you you start
learning to manage a team,

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:56.300
to manage resources,

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.080
to think in multi-year time horizons,

00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:59.850
it's a really important step

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:02.410
for us to all go through.

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:03.770
And when I hear people tell me

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:06.360
that they want to make
an impact on the world

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:07.360
and they go straight

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:10.080
from you know high school to that

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:12.330
or sometimes straight from college to that

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:14.170
and they don't get a
little experience working

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:15.830
in the entrepreneurial world

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:17.110
my heart sinks a little bit

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:18.500
because I think they're not going to be

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:20.620
as powerful at making a difference

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:21.620
or an impact in the world

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.060
as they would have been had they gone

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:24.700
and made themselves strong

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:27.860
and powerful and successful first.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:30.760
Start habitualizing or ritualizing

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:34.230
or systemizing or
routineizing those things

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:36.060
that are the most important things

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:39.190
and start doing them every
day at the same time.

00:09:39.190 --> 00:09:40.610
And what you'll find

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:42.600
is that especially in the work arena,

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:45.470
in business, if you will make rituals

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:48.340
and routines out of the
very high value things

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:50.060
in your life every day,

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:52.760
you'll do them at the
same time automatically

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:54.890
because if you think about it

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:57.600
you already do the same things

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:01.840
every day at the same time automatically.

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:03.360
When we procrastinate

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:04.570
what we're usually doing

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:06.860
is resisting doing something different

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:08.390
than we normally do.

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:10.610
Right we have our routines that we're in.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:11.810
We're all creatures of habit.

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:13.160
We'd like to do the same things

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:14.890
at around the same times every day.

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:16.440
And when we're procrastinating

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:17.440
what we're doing is going

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:18.510
oh I don't really want to do

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:19.910
that thing right now.

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:20.910
Sometimes we don't know why.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:22.470
We're coming up with a bunch of excuses.

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:24.350
It's usually just
because it's not a habit.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:25.350
It's not a routine.

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:27.540
It's not something that
we do automatically

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:28.910
every day.

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:30.060
As an example

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:31.750
I struggled for years

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:34.020
with trying to get my sleep

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:36.500
and my exercise and my diet

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.040
all in shape.

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:39.040
Well that all changed

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:41.700
when I built a simple routine

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:45.230
where I go to sleep at the same time.

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:47.260
I wake up around the same time

00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:49.190
and then I do my exercise first thing

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:51.570
and then I eat a healthy meal first thing.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:53.760
And then I just made
a routine out of that.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:54.760
So I go to sleep.

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:56.230
I get enough sleep.

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:57.580
I wake up.

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:58.580
First thing that I do

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:00.360
is I make sure that I get my exercise

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:02.380
and then I have a healthy meal.

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:03.540
And now I'm pulled

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:05.520
into these routines every day

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:07.020
and I don't have to worry

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:08.800
about procrastinating

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:10.110
because it's a ritual.

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:11.950
It's something that I
do the same everyday.

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:13.620
Now it takes 30 days or so

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.630
to actually create a new habit.

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:18.000
So you got to force yourself to do it

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:19.850
at the same time every day.

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:21.140
At 2 to 3 weeks

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:22.670
you'll notice it gets easier and easier.

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:24.070
And then in about a month

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:26.230
you're just doing the
exact same thing every day.

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:27.270
You're pulled into it.

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:29.010
You find yourself doing it automatically.

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:31.250
And this is the one where everyone goes

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.170
I don't want to be a salesperson right.

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:34.290
You know one of the things

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:35.410
that we do in our business

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:37.520
is we take experts

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:39.010
and we teach them how to package

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.380
their information up into products

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.700
like ebooks and other information products

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:45.270
and sell them.

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:47.420
Well when I start talking to these experts

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:50.570
almost universally they say things like

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:51.820
I've got all the content,

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:53.560
I just need to find someone

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:56.360
who can market and sell it for me.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:57.360
And when I say to them

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.810
well you know what would probably be good

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:00.890
for you is to actually
learn some marketing

00:12:00.890 --> 00:12:01.890
and sales they go

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:04.830
oh I don't want to learn.

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:06.240
I'm not a salesman.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.310
They kind of like look
down at sales people

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:10.180
like it's some like lower form

00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:13.320
of human business scum
or something like that.

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:16.120
And you know you imagine okay

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:18.380
I have to put on a funky like a weird suit

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:19.620
and like a windbreaker

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:21.630
like a car salesman in
order to sell my product.

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.850
I would never want to do that.

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:26.290
Well when you really learn sales

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:27.290
as I know you know

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:29.150
because you're a fantastic salesperson

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:32.240
that the best selling methods

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:33.940
are consultative selling

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:34.990
where you don't sit down

00:12:34.990 --> 00:12:36.870
and try to talk someone into buying.

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:37.910
You sit down and you say

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:39.520
let me ask you some questions.

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:40.520
Let me learn about you

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:42.320
and find out what all your problems are

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:45.380
and let me see if what
I have is even a fit.

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:46.530
And then once you've found out

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:48.690
where they're at, what their problems are,

00:12:48.690 --> 00:12:50.260
what all the challenges
they're facing are,

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:51.820
what they'd like to accomplish,

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:53.920
then you sell solutions.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:56.660
You sell them fixing their problems.

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:58.820
You sell them getting what they want

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:00.580
not your thing.

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:04.170
And the best of the best
of the best salespeople

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:05.630
are the ones that walk in, sit down

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:07.000
and ask a bunch of questions

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:09.160
and then say my product can't help you,

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:10.890
let me refer you to someone who can,

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:11.940
because those are the people

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:13.330
that win the trust

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:14.980
and that when they say

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:16.820
this is the thing that
will solve your problem

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:19.290
the prospect says that's the thing I need

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:20.290
because they're trustworthy.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:21.970
So learning consultative selling

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:24.270
and really learning how to
sell like a professional

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:25.410
is very important.

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:27.980
Know thyself.

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:29.720
Know thyself:

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:31.660
this is probably the most famous phrase

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.690
handed down from the Greek philosophers.

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:36.940
Know thyself;

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:38.390
Why is it so important?

00:13:38.390 --> 00:13:39.970
Why is it so profound?

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:42.270
And another question.

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:44.810
Why do we do what we do?

00:13:44.810 --> 00:13:46.750
Why do we think the way we think?

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:49.110
Why do we feel the way we feel?

00:13:49.110 --> 00:13:51.000
Why do we behave in certain patterns

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.110
and get into certain relationship patterns

00:13:53.110 --> 00:13:54.630
in our lives?

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:56.560
Well these are the magic questions.

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:58.940
Psychology answers these questions

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:00.380
on the general level

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:02.230
but we all have experiences

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:04.170
that are private very individual

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:05.620
and very powerful.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:06.640
We have something

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:08.470
that's shaping our thoughts,

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:09.820
shaping our emotions,

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:13.430
shaping our behavior from the inside.

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:16.000
Why is it so important to know yourself?

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.000
What does it mean?

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.570
Well I don't think it means

00:14:18.570 --> 00:14:20.660
to know what your favorite TV show is

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:22.540
or what your favorite restaurant is.

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:24.230
I do think to know yourself means

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:25.810
to understand your personality,

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:28.450
to understand how you're wired,

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.500
what you're likely to do
in different situations,

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:32.000
under different types of pressure

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:34.130
and with different types of people.

00:14:34.130 --> 00:14:37.050
The reason that it's so
important to know thyself

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:38.050
is because there are many

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:40.210
different types of people in the world

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:41.520
and to create success

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.930
you must work effectively with yourself

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:44.930
and with others.

00:14:44.930 --> 00:14:46.110
You must know yourself.

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.370
You must know how you work

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:49.240
so you can control yourself,

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:50.240
communicate well

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:52.360
and understand what
others are communicating

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:54.490
and ultimately increase your effectiveness

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:56.540
communicating and persuading others

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:57.630
and creating the results

00:14:57.630 --> 00:14:59.290
that you want in your life.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.630
It's also critical to know yourself

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:02.810
so you can understand your weaknesses,

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:05.450
your soft spots, your Achilles heels

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:07.040
and those things in your life

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:08.530
that can hurt you.

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:11.000
All of these things are
intimately connected

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:13.610
to your personality.

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:14.860
Understanding your personality

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:16.690
is understanding yourself.

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:18.640
If you'd like to know thyself

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:20.420
then know thy personality.

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:22.740
In the past the paradigm that we use

00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:24.880
as business owners and marketers

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:27.600
is that we have some entry-level stuff

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:29.470
that we use to get prospects' attention.

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:31.800
And those things might
be like advertisements

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:33.100
or we might offer you know

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:34.100
some free information

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:35.100
or a free report

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:37.080
or sometimes even free recorded messages

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:38.860
or free consultations.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:39.860
And then we move

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:41.830
and we have the kind of
mid-level priced products

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:43.630
that we sell and upsell to.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:45.270
And then we have our highest end products

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:47.360
that we sell to our best customers.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:48.770
Well what's happening now

00:15:48.770 --> 00:15:50.000
and what's happening a lot

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:51.920
and accelerating over the last few years

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:53.680
with the rise of the Internet

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.370
is more and more stuff
is available for free.

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:58.080
There are more companies

00:15:58.080 --> 00:15:59.920
that are funded by venture capital

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:02.770
that have 50 million
dollars in cash in the bank

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:03.880
that they don't know what to do with.

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:06.660
So they're just giving
stuff away to customers.

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:07.660
Things are becoming cheaper

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:08.660
and cheaper to produce.

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:09.790
And all that stuff

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:10.910
that you used to think of

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:13.550
as being your real valuable stuff,

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:14.550
now you've got your competitors

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.700
giving it away to your customers.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:19.160
So if you can't beat them
you need to join them.

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:20.430
And in fact what I think you need to do

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:21.700
is get in front of them.

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:22.980
And what we do

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:25.190
is we take that line,

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:26.190
that was the stuff

00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:28.290
that we used to give away for free

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:29.310
and we move it deeper

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:31.830
into the customer relationship.

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:32.830
And the things

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:34.090
that we used to charge money for,

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:35.620
our entry-level products,

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:36.910
now we give away.

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:38.440
And what that does

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:41.190
is it builds relationships
with more customers.

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:43.690
It allows us to kind of widen our funnel

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:44.890
so to speak

00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:47.750
and attract a lot more prospects.

00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:48.750
So let me give you an example

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:50.980
from one of our current businesses.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.310
As I mentioned before we have a company

00:16:52.310 --> 00:16:53.540
called Double Your Dating.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:54.580
And in that company

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:57.020
we teach dating advice to men.

00:16:57.020 --> 00:16:58.020
Now we actually have another company

00:16:58.020 --> 00:16:59.380
that we teach dating advice to women

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:00.380
and we have others

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:01.380
that we teach other kind of self-help

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:03.770
and personal development topics.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:04.860
But the one that started it all

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:06.850
was the company called Double your Dating.

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:08.100
And when I originally sat down

00:17:08.100 --> 00:17:11.830
to work on the marketing for that company

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:15.150
I started playing around
with email newsletters.

00:17:15.150 --> 00:17:16.310
And at first the newsletters

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:17.780
that I sent out were very short

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:18.780
and there were excerpts

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:20.160
of some of our products

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:23.260
and other stuff that wasn't
really all that valuable

00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:24.260
but it was free

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:25.260
and I thought that people

00:17:25.260 --> 00:17:27.830
would you know kind of
find some value in it.

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:29.350
We started sending them out.

00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:31.620
Well as we developed I
started writing longer

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:33.570
and longer newsletters and I realized

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:35.980
that the more valuable the newsletter

00:17:35.980 --> 00:17:37.300
the more it caused people

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:39.030
to want to invest in our products.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:41.690
And at one point I said to myself

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:42.690
you know what,

00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:44.970
I want to create the
most valuable newsletter

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:46.360
that has ever been created

00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:49.590
on any topic ever in history

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:51.280
and then I want to give it away.

00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:53.530
I set the bar very high.

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:54.730
And when I was thinking this

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:56.550
I was thinking about financial newsletters

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.750
that sometimes cost
thousands of dollars a year.

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:01.000
I mean I was really
putting the bar up there.

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.970
And if you've ever read
some of our newsletters

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:04.130
you'll see that they average

00:18:04.130 --> 00:18:06.020
probably fifteen or twenty pages long

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.020
and we send them out

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:08.020
every couple of days.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:10.830
Some of them are as long as 30 or 40 pages

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:14.440
of value jam-packed with entertaining,

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:17.540
useful, step-by-step, mindsets,

00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:19.490
everything that you could possibly need.

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:20.490
And we get letters

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:21.490
from all around the world

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:24.790
constantly talking of appreciation,

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.450
thanking us for the value that we jam-pack

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:27.450
into these newsletters.

00:18:27.450 --> 00:18:29.100
If you subscribe to that newsletter

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:31.240
and you're interested
in getting dating advice

00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:34.240
you will have your pitcher
filled up to the brim.

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:36.200
Now, I recommend that you ask yourself

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:38.920
how can you move the free
line in your business?

00:18:38.920 --> 00:18:40.940
You might not want to
go overboard like we did

00:18:40.940 --> 00:18:42.940
but what's an entry level product

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:45.010
that doesn't cost you much to produce

00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:47.780
that you can just give
away to your customers?

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:49.470
If you don't use information products

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:52.170
in your business, things
like email newsletters,

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:54.280
and downloadable ebooks,

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:56.140
and CD and DVD courses,

00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:57.550
and streaming video

00:18:57.550 --> 00:18:58.880
like you're watching right now,

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:00.470
then you really need to do that

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:01.690
and you need to learn about it

00:19:01.690 --> 00:19:03.370
as soon as you possibly can.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:07.480
The idea of bringing light to failures.

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:08.480
Right and you mentioned

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:09.480
that in our business

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:10.480
we try to encourage people

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:11.480
as soon as you see something

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:12.480
that goes wrong

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:13.480
or you screw something up

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:14.480
raise your hand

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:15.480
and say hey I screwed-up

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:16.480
or I see something that's wrong over here

00:19:16.480 --> 00:19:17.480
and make it a win.

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:19.210
And I just want to just
slip this in there.

00:19:19.210 --> 00:19:21.370
The reason why that's so important

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:23.470
is that we humans don't like

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:25.120
to look bad in front of others.

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:26.330
We don't like to look like idiots.

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:28.410
We don't like to screw things up.

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:30.280
So what we do in a business

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:31.690
or a corporate environment

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:33.850
is we screw something up

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:35.240
and then we take it and we hide it

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:36.420
and we isolate.

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:38.130
We try to not let anyone see it.

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:40.910
We try to go to work fixing it.

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:42.120
Unfortunately if you've
screwed something up

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:43.120
it probably means

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:44.120
that you didn't know

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:45.480
how to do it right the first time

00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:47.000
and it probably also means further

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:49.470
that if you take it and
isolate and try to fix it

00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:50.850
you're probably going
to even make it worse.

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:54.590
And if you let people have that mentality

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:56.210
of you're going to get in trouble

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:57.710
if you screw something up

00:19:57.710 --> 00:19:58.710
they're going to isolate.

00:19:58.710 --> 00:19:59.710
They're going to go try to fix it.

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:00.710
They're going to make it worse

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:01.710
and then when they show up

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:03.210
and it gets discovered

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:04.490
they might try to use a scapegoat

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:05.640
and say it wasn't my fault

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:07.600
or someone else did it.

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:09.580
And you know it's just
a really bad situation.

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:11.630
So if you can make an environment

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:14.470
or culture where finding screw-ups,

00:20:14.470 --> 00:20:17.590
raising your hand when
something goes wrong,

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:19.900
saying I made a mistake is a win

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:23.050
and the person to spot
the screw-up the fastest

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:24.880
is the biggest winner,

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:27.210
then I think you can
move forward very quickly

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:29.710
and you can as W. Edwards Deming said

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:31.340
you can drive out fear

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:32.700
which is one of the most important things

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:33.700
you can do in an organization.

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:35.360
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:36.360
